{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/66909-artifacts-relics-and-hunters","id":66909,"title":"Artifacts, Relics and Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-06T19:29:01-08:00","id":66909,"title":"Artifacts, Relics and Hunters","content":"So, correct me if I'm wrong, but I imagine that the various compacts and conspiracies spend time bringing in a variety of non sentient supernatural stuff, things like relics. Cheiron probably can find a way to make money off them, TFV could very well run a Warehouse 13 kind of place...am I off base on this? Is there a book or anything on Relic hunters besides Relics (duh)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T21:44:10-08:00","id":66980,"title":"","content":"Aside from Aegis Kai Doru?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T09:04:47-08:00","id":67229,"title":"","content":"Right. Maybe even tier 1 hunters tracking down weirdness that ends up being an artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T14:29:39-08:00","id":67416,"title":"","content":"There's the Reliquary book. My game revolved around thieves before they became vampires (now they're vampire thieves).<br /> Honestly, I didn't like Reliquary.<br /> The new Mummy book came out, though, and it has a bunch of magical relics. They're relic hunters, too.<br /> Vampires and Aegis Kai Doru and a few other groups have places they hold magic item stuff, but there's just mentions of them, not like a full book on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T17:15:33-08:00","id":67491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/66909-artifacts-relics-and-hunters#post66909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, correct me if I'm wrong, but I imagine that the various compacts and conspiracies spend time bringing in a variety of non sentient supernatural stuff, things like relics. Cheiron probably can find a way to make money off them, TFV could very well run a Warehouse 13 kind of place...am I off base on this? Is there a book or anything on Relic hunters besides Relics (duh)?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of them other than AKD make Artifacts/Relics/whatever a top-priority, and certainly none of the others actively equip their own Hunters with them. Which is not to say that an individual Hunter can not have a cool-plot-hook cursed/blessed/whatever item. The thing is it's going to be an individual story hook itself, as opposed to a general Endowment like the stuff AKD has the resources to outfit its hunters with.<br /> <br /> Yes, as far as I'm concerned, VALKYRIE does have a Vault in their underground Arizona facility where recovered arcane materials are stored. Similarly, Malleus does have some Holy Relics, but has Benedictions specifically for the safe destruction of unholy items (i.e. magical items that don't qualify as Holy Relics). Again, a Hunter wielding one of these items is a specific plot-hook situation, not a general Endowment like with Aegis Kai Doru.<br /> <br /> Cheiron I'd say does not have, but would very much LIKE, the secrets that Last Dynasty International uses to harvest Sekhem for drugs from destroying relics. Other than that, relics don't have a special interest for them, unless the specific item has healing, psychological, or bio-transmutative properties that might be studied. In any event, it's all for research for other applications purposes if brought back, not something they'd directly use in Thaumatechnology necessarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:22:17-08:00","id":68040,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd take note of how the monsters deal with the problem. The Mysterium for example has a multitude of locations for storage of artefacts, as putting them together makes them a massive target, no matter how much fortification you put around it. On a related note, there's the Green Box system from Delta Green; the group pays for a load of self-storage units scattered across the country and then uses them to store any odds and ends they have. Stealth is a lot cheaper than paying for armed guards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T15:39:51-08:00","id":68118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/66909-artifacts-relics-and-hunters?p=68040#post68040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd take note of how the monsters deal with the problem. The Mysterium for example has a multitude of locations for storage of artefacts, as putting them together makes them a massive target, no matter how much fortification you put around it. On a related note, there's the Green Box system from Delta Green; the group pays for a load of self-storage units scattered across the country and then uses them to store any odds and ends they have. Stealth is a lot cheaper than paying for armed guards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Headcanon accepted for how VALKYRIE handles general ENOs (Extra-Normal Objects); however, dangerous enough ones (or ones that might be of use designing Advanced Armory) would definitely get shipped to Arizona IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T18:05:15-08:00","id":68173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/66909-artifacts-relics-and-hunters?p=67416#post67416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> The new Mummy book came out, though, and it has a bunch of magical relics. They're relic hunters, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arisen relics tend to have the nasty habit of sucking the soul out of mortals. You would have to house rule them to make them less scary for Hunters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T07:03:55-08:00","id":68403,"title":"","content":"To make them less scary for hunters to <i>use,</i> yes. They're just right for hunters who think of them as a supernatural menace and want to warehouse or destroy them, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T03:18:27-07:00","id":89372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/66909-artifacts-relics-and-hunters?p=68173#post68173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arisen relics tend to have the nasty habit of sucking the soul out of mortals. You would have to house rule them to make them less scary for Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a bit misleading, they all already have curses attached to them, they work as is. You can use the Olympian Frog for instance without worrying about losing your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}